00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello there it's been a hot minute since  we had our first official look at god of  war ragnarok the follow-up to the  record-breaking 2018 smash which took  kratos away from the greek pantheon and  into the realm of norse mythology in  those three years kratos has been  playing fortnite a lot with loki and  thor but alas it's time to get down to  the real business of breaking down the  god of war ragnarok trailer to look at  33 things you may have missed let's do  this oh and if you haven't finished the  2018 game please click off now because  spoilers are coming boy  the trailer begins with the return of  atreus from a successful hunt his  silhouette is framed to show antlers  from the top of his head to quickly  remind us atreyus has a pseudonym to go  by loki we found out three years ago  atreus is both the son of the god of war  kratos and the son of a frost giant  another cool thing to note about the  opening shot is its similarity to the  first game in which kratos teaches  atreus to hunt but he's unable to put  down the deer without help in god of war  ragnarok atreus has no such issues  anymore and can hunt all alone oh and i  guess now is a good time to confirm at  least three years have passed in game  kratos may look the same but atreus has  shot up so much he now towers the dwarfs  he once stood among in the same scene  later in the trailer we also see kratos  holding this pouch it may seem strange  but this is a reminder of his last task  to scatter his wife's ashes at the end  of the 2018 game  it's here to show he misses her greatly  and even though their task is over he  continues to think of her  the first line of the trailer is given  to atreus time is running out  the prophecies say final winter leads to  ragnarok time is running out indeed as  the name suggests god of war ragnarok is  following closely to the norse prophecy  of ragnarok and this includes thimble  winter a frost that precedes the end of  the world and puts an end to all life on  the planet in game this has  ramifications for us all including our  gameplay the boat we use will not always  be available to move around the island  and instead a new mode of transport is  confirmed the wolf driven sled for those  that like names these two wolves are  called specky and swana the lake is now  a sheet of ice as the days pass by to  the end of all existence  we've spotted a few locations from the  original game in here which are now  overrun with snow but if you like me and  you don't like snow in video games it's  all good not every realm is like this  speaking of realms in the original 2018  game we visited six of the nine norse  myth realms and now during ragnarok it  is confirmed we will have access to all  nine realms the ones we haven't been to  so far swaddlheim where the dwarves call  home vanaheim the realm of the veneer  gods and asgard the home of thor led by  his father king odin and speaking of  odin he's always been watching us  through the eyes of his ravens hugin and  munin who can be spotted in the trailer  a few times oh and look the transcended  ravens are here too confirming that  collectibles from the 2018 game are  likely returning next we see the return  of freyja the witch in the woods is now  a key antagonist to kratos and atreus as  they travel through ragnarok freyja was  our ally in 2018 healing atreus who  would have died without her in return  for saving our son kratos murders her  son that was a touching moment okay it  didn't play out just like that but that  is why freya is now the enemy let's  break it down a little her son balder  still a baby was destined to die so  freya used her witching ways to protect  him from death causing him to be immune  from any kind of harm but this was  actually a curse and not a gift balder  lost all feelings which led him to go  down a dark path of hatred towards his  mother in a freak incident mistletoe was  the ingredient needed to reverse  baldur's immunity to feelings and pain  and well you know the rest to save  freya's life kratos gave chiropractic  assistance  freya's guilt then became an obsession  with revenge and that's why she will be  around often to foil us in god of war  ragnarok i will parade your cold body  from every corner  of every realm  and feed your soul to the vilest filth  in hell that is my promise he saved your  life he robbed me of everything  there's one issue we should really note  in 2018 we were told that odin cursed  freya to never be able to harm a living  creature for as long as she lived  well as you can see that isn't true  anymore so this should confirm odin will  be in the game as he is the only one  with the power to remove that curse  the other main villain of the piece is  none other than thor the visions kratos  saw at the end of the previous game are  almost exactly the same as the reality  when thor comes to visit  of course atreus is older and finally  thor answers kratos's question vaguely  are you a calm and reasonable person  [Music]  thor will be played by none other than  ryan hurst a man worthy of norse  immortality you may recognize him from  sons of anarchy in which he played opie  and more recently he played beta in the  walking dead thor is confirmed to have a  dad bod like he does in north mythology  so take away your aussie blonde thor and  give me a fat norwegian redhead please  chef kiss next on the trailer we finally  meet the god of war tia this is the  third god of war we know of the first  was ares in the greek pantheon who  kratos overthrew and now tia is the  norse version who is hella tall tear was  spoken of in the previous games and  helped the giants who opposed odin  although he was a god of war he promoted  peace and stopped wars rather than  starting them unlike kratos and now it  seems he's alive and well and hella tall  in norse mythology tia had his hand  bitten off by fenrir who so happens to  be the son of loki which suggests time  travel will be possible in god of war  ragnarok because yoman gander the world  serpent is also a child of loki oh and a  cool nod to this is seen on the clasp of  atreus's bow it's shaped like an s like  the serpent foreshadowing his connection  to yomenganda very cool detail before we  speak about the final character in  ragnarok let's quickly look over a few  gameplay changes coming we are set to  use the blades of chaos like a grappling  hook to quickly ascend to new areas and  the same weapon is used to propel us  forward into enemies our shield has been  given an upgrade in ragnarok the  circular shield is here but it's also  replaced with an oval shield and a more  roman looking rectangular shield too  this either confirms the shield will be  customizable or there will be multiple  shields to find and utilize differently  both options sound damn good to me in  one shot atreus can be seen riding a  mount but not just any mount it's a  summoned mount proving he is aging and  controlling his powers more as each day  passes and i'm hopeful that one day we  will play as loki i mean atreus i mean  loki you get what i mean  we also get a few new enemy types to  look at this crocodile thing is said to  be a dreki which is the old norse word  for dragon and i got to admit it i'd  prefer to fight them at this stage and  not when they're a fully grown adult  another enemy is the stalker which looks  an awful lot like a centaur from greek  mythology this is not worthy because as  far as i'm aware nor smith doesn't  include centaurs well in fact there is  the knuckle av but that thing is more  like a horror movie villain frightening  but the biggest gameplay update in the  new trailer is this mamiya's new ability  to turn pages of a book with a spoon  mind-blowing this is how sequels are  made from the subsequent interviews with  god of war developers here are a couple  of other things you should really know  corey barlog is no longer the director  of ragnarok he has stood down from his  role to pursue other ventures but will  be there to support the new director  eric williams eric has worked on all the  god of war games to date which tells us  the project is in good hands another  bombshell we have had confirmed is that  god of war ragnarok is the end of the  north series for kratos only two games  and not the trilogy we all expected it's  kind of a bummer but these games take so  long to make that it's a great deal of  dedication for a single team to give for  over a decade on the plus side the story  of odin will now be present in ragnarok  instead of saved for the third game how  do you feel about that and do you think  odin will simply be a side character or  one of the main villains and finally on  to another new character angra boda who  in north myth is the bringer of grief  that sounds great doesn't it but look at  her she looks like butter wouldn't melt  angravada is the soulmate of loki and  the mother of monsters such as yoman  gander and fenrir can you see what i'm  getting at here atreus and this young  lady are the parents of beings thousands  of years old which once again leads me  to believe a form of time travel magic  will be key to this story it's unclear  if this young lady will be a straight up  love interest for atreus or hopefully  something much more difficult to define  and let's leave her with the final say  you'll get your answer soon enough  well some of them  answers are coming i'm adam you're  awesome i'll see you next time  [Music]  you

